  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 140 PM CDT Sun Jul 26 2026\n\nAs of 1:30pm, the coolest heat index in the CWA is the 108 \nreading at Wayne, NE. Most temps are in the mid-90s with \ndewpoints generally in the upper 70s. It is hot and it is humid.\n\nModels are converging on a solution that brings an MCS through \nthe area this evening from about Yankton and fizzling out around\nI-80. The RAP and the HRRR are still keeping things mostly dry.\nConsider the severe threat tonight to be conditional, meaning \nif storms are able to develop, they should be able to grow \nvolatile. Whether they develop or not is not certain (60%). \nIt'll be hard to produce hail with temps as warm as they are, \nbut shear and instability magnitudes suggest organized \ndevelopment is possible. Damaging winds will be the primary \nthreat with decreasing severity as the storms push southeast. \nBy the time they push through the Fremont/Omaha areas, they \nshould begin to weaken... if they are to develop at all. \nTornadoes can be all but ruled out. Expect dry conditions by 5am\nas remaining action should be in Missouri by then.",
